From df5392341552261313672129419605937dea0dea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:35:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 075/144] drm/msm/dp: don't take extra references on multiple
 plug events

The upper layers might signal multiple sequential HPD plug events. Don't
take extra references and skip all further HPD plug events until we
receive the unplug event.

Fixes: 3ea2d1c3d154 ("drm/msm/dp: turn link_ready into plugged")
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Message-ID: <20261024-hpd-irq-events-v8-6-6ee949e7a384@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024-hpd-irq-events-v8-6-6ee949e7a384@oss.qualcomm.com/

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0097-drm-msm-dp-don-t-take-extra-references-on-multiple-p.patch
Import-SHA256: 947ab3168a25b0183e06f37bba3d8ff9a4cbc5fe7ec72b8d4b41503b64265dde
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit 12c28099a5c65b463378bcade5c56b4c70271dba)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 4dcbd9b99d..ae5a1674cf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -411,6 +411,9 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
 
+	if (dp->plugged)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
